.TH markdown-viewer 1  "markdown-viewer 0.15.1" 
.SH NAME
markdown\-viewer \- Render a Markdown file with GitHub styling and live\-reload it in your browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmarkdown\-viewer\fR [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-watch\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-pdf\fR] [\fB\-\-clipboard\fR] [\fB\-\-goto\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-running\fR] [\fB\-\-check\-links\fR] [\fB\-\-diff\fR] [\fB\-\-recent\fR] [\fB\-\-online\fR] [\fB\-\-lint\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-open\fR] [\fB\-\-browser\fR] [\fB\-\-app\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-tab\fR] [\fB\-\-exit\-when\-closed\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-running\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-finder\fR] [\fB\-\-uninstall\-finder\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-desktop\fR] [\fB\-\-uninstall\-desktop\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-style\fR] [\fB\-\-css\fR] [\fB\-\-number\-headings\fR] [\fB\-\-line\-numbers\fR] [\fB\-\-front\-matter\fR] [\fB\-\-obsidian\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-obsidian\fR] [\fB\-\-editor\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIFILE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render a Markdown file with GitHub styling and live\-reload it in your browser
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-watch\fR
Serve the page and live\-reload it whenever the file changes
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write the rendered HTML to this file ("\-" for stdout) instead of opening it. For a folder, write a static site into this folder
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write a PDF to this file instead of opening it (needs Chrome, Chromium, Edge, Brave or Vivaldi)
.TP
\fB\-\-clipboard\fR
Preview the clipboard instead of a file. With \-\-watch, the page follows the clipboard as it changes
.TP
\fB\-\-goto\fR \fI<FILE:LINE>\fR
Scroll a running viewer to FILE:LINE, starting one if needed. For editor commands (see editors/ in the repository)
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-running\fR
With \-\-goto: do nothing if no viewer is showing the file (for editors following the cursor, so a closed preview stays closed)
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-links\fR
Check links and images in FILE (or every Markdown file in a folder) and report broken ones; exits with status 1 if any are
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Show FILE with what changed since a git revision marked: added text in green, removed text struck through in red (e.g. \-\-diff HEAD for uncommitted changes, \-\-diff HEAD~3, \-\-diff main)
.TP
\fB\-\-recent\fR
Show the files and folders you opened recently (also what you get with no FILE in your home folder)
.TP
\fB\-\-online\fR
With \-\-check\-links: also check web links (needs curl)
.TP
\fB\-\-lint\fR
Report writing problems in FILE (or every Markdown file in a folder): skipped heading levels, images without alt text, empty links and more; exits with status 1 if there are any. Combines with \-\-check\-links
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Port for \-\-watch (default: any free port)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-open\fR
Don\*(Aqt open a browser
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Browser to open instead of the default (e.g. "Google Chrome", "firefox")
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR
Open as a minimal app window with no tabs or address bar (default). Chrome, Edge, Brave, Chromium and Vivaldi only; other browsers get a new window
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR
Open in a normal new browser window
.TP
\fB\-\-tab\fR
Open in a tab of an existing browser window
.TP
\fB\-\-exit\-when\-closed\fR
With \-\-watch: exit once the page has been closed, even with \-\-no\-open (used by the Finder integration). Without \-\-no\-open, this is the default
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-running\fR
With \-\-watch: keep serving after the window is closed (until Ctrl\-C)
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-finder\fR
macOS: add "Markdown Viewer" to Finder (Open With, double\-click and a right\-click Quick Action) for the current user
.TP
\fB\-\-uninstall\-finder\fR
macOS: remove the Finder integration
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-desktop\fR
Linux: add "Markdown Viewer" to your desktop\*(Aqs applications, for Open With on Markdown, CSV and TSV files (current user only)
.TP
\fB\-\-uninstall\-desktop\fR
Linux: remove the desktop integration
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR
Colour theme (default: the one you last chose in the viewer, else auto). Press t in the viewer to switch
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Follow the operating system\*(Aqs light/dark setting
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR \fI<STYLE>\fR
Page style
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
github: GitHub\*(Aqs README look
.IP \(bu 2
wide: GitHub\*(Aqs look, using the full window width
.IP \(bu 2
book: Serif type and a narrower column, for long\-form reading
.IP \(bu 2
compact: Smaller type and tighter spacing, for dense documents
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-css\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Extra CSS file, applied after the built\-in styles
.TP
\fB\-\-number\-headings\fR
Number headings (1, 1.1, 1.2, …)
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-numbers\fR
Number the lines of every code block (or per block, with `showLineNumbers` in its info string)
.TP
\fB\-\-front\-matter\fR \fI<HOW>\fR
YAML front matter: shown as a table, like GitHub (default), or hidden
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Show it as a table, like GitHub
.IP \(bu 2
hide: Leave it out
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-obsidian\fR
Obsidian notes: [[wiki links]], ![[embeds]], callouts, ==highlights== and %%comments%%. On by default inside a vault (a .obsidian folder)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-obsidian\fR
Turn off Obsidian notes, even inside a vault
.TP
\fB\-\-editor\fR \fI<COMMAND>\fR
Editor for double\-click\-to\-source, e.g. "zed" or "code \-g {file}:{line}" (default: $VISUAL/$EDITOR if it\*(Aqs a GUI editor, else the first one found)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Markdown file to render, a folder to browse (default: the current folder), a web address (https://…, including GitHub and GitLab file and repository pages), or "\-" to read standard input. Folders are always served with live reload
.SH VERSION
v0.15.1
